  "description": "Shinga is a pair of spiral climbers shaped like a bull's horns, facing each other across a wavy balance path that forms the head. Children climb up a horn from either side, meet in the middle and cross over, so two groups play towards each other. The photos show it in Play Orange on a grass mound, and Cherry Red is also offered. The age range is 5 to 12, with room for 15 children. The climber is long and narrow, 22'10\" x 4'9\", with a safe play area of 27'10\" x 9'9\". Climbing and balancing build interaction and parallel play. Its galvanised pipe and moulded parts carry our 3-year warranty. Ask us whether a mound or a flat base suits your site.",
